course: dictionary
lesson: 7402
title: What is a poem?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A poem is writing set out in lines, often with rhythm and sometimes rhyme. A poet writes one to share feelings or ideas in a special, beautiful way. «Poems paint pictures with words, called imagery.» So as you read, look for the pictures forming in your mind.
explain: Poems can be any length and any mood. A poem can be funny, sad, short like a haiku or long like a ballad. Ask yourself: what is the poet trying to make me feel?
explain: The sound matters too. «Faster than fairies, faster than witches, / Bridges and houses, hedges and ditches» has a quick beat, like wheels on a track. A sad poem is read slowly and softly, so the rhythm can match the meaning.
fact: A poem is a piece of writing in lines.
fact: Many poems have rhythm, and some also have rhyme.
fact: A poem can be funny, sad, short or long.
fact: «Poems paint pictures with words, called imagery.»
fact: An acrostic poem spells a word with the first letter of each line, and each line should be a phrase, not just one word.
exercise: What is a poem? | A letter sent to a friend in another town | *A piece of writing in lines, often with rhythm and sometimes rhyme | A map showing where to walk | A list of shopping items with prices
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Poems paint pictures with words, called imagery.» that names the pictures in a poem. | *imagery | paint | words | poems
exercise: What does an acrostic poem spell? | A list of rhyming words | A song sung by a choir | *A word, using the first letter of each line | A long story told in plain sentences
test: In «Faster than fairies, faster than witches», what does the quick beat make the poem feel like? | *Wheels rattling along a track | A goldfish swimming | A slow walk in the park | A sleepy night
test: Which kind of poem can be long? | Limerick with only one line | Acrostic that spells one word | *Ballad | Haiku
exam: Why might a sad poem be read slowly and softly? | Because the poet forgot the rhythm | Because poems must always be read quietly | Because slow words are easier to spell | *Because the rhythm matches the sad meaning
